A||||11||turbo86se||Real bad alignment?||||14||
Z||000000||turbo86se||10-31-2001||12:04 PM||||I just got my '88 coupe back from the shop. As some of you know, last week the two bolts holding the f/r caliper came off, sending my caliper into the wheel, locking it up. The caliper had a nice crack on it too. I had my f/r caliper replaced, and had the shop install new shocks while they were in there. <P>I just drove the car, and it pulls to the right sharply. It tracks horribly, and the steering wheel is way to the left. I can feel it trying to pull right slightly while driving. Before last week, it handled like it was on rails, even with bad shocks, and the alignment was super straight.<P>Does it sound like I need just an alignment? Or is there something else wrong in there?<P>You guys are the best! TIA! <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||turbo86se||10-31-2001||01:50 PM||||Bump!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-31-2001||01:54 PM||||Bent tie rod?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||10-31-2001||02:03 PM||||Sounds like something got bent. Tie rod would be the most likely. I also saw someone post on here that even though the knuckle is cast it can bend. Alignment definitely needs done. It should be checked carefully for damaged parts first though. A good alignment shop should be able to check it all out if you let them know the history.||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||10-31-2001||02:55 PM||||Thanks DRH and Indiana, I've got the car up on ramps now. What should I be looking for? Do you think it would be the inner or outer tie rod?<P>Thanks again!||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||10-31-2001||03:08 PM||||Ok, something is definitly not right. The f/r wheel is not straight up and down. It leans inward, towards the top of the car. This is what I noticed as my Fiero skidded off the road, but couldn't tell b/c of the angle it was on. <BR>Maybe steering knuckle or spindle?<BR>Damn I hope not! Getting it back cost enough!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Banzai||10-31-2001||04:49 PM||||Do you have adjustable upper ball joints?? It's possible they slipped. Or possibly broke a bolt on the stock one.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||10-31-2001||05:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Banzai:<BR><B>Do you have adjustable upper ball joints?? It's possible they slipped. Or possibly broke a bolt on the stock one.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DITO||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||10-31-2001||05:14 PM||||Adjustable upper ball joints? I doubt it. It's whatever came from the factory. Ed Parks said it may be the upper control arm or the pivot bar that attaches to the subframe. It may be bent.<P>Would this mean I'd need to replace the upper ball joints? Aren't they extinct?<BR>Will I do any harm to anything other than the tire if I drive it to a shop and back?<BR>Thanks!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||DRH||10-31-2001||05:15 PM||||On an 88 the whole upper control arm can be moved around to adjust caster and camber by loosening the two bolts that hold the upper control arm shaft to the front cradle. It's possible you just wedged the caliper in hard enough to knock it out of adjustment without bending or breaking anything. Look at where the upper control arm shaft bolts down and see if it looks like it slid in.<P>It could also have bent the upper control arm, bent or broken the upper control arm shaft, bent the lower control arm, knocked a ball joint loose, or possibly bent the knuckle. Look at everything closely for anything that is obviously bent and compare to the other side if neccessary. <P>You will definitely need an alignment. If you can't find anything else wrong make sure the shop knows what happened so they can check everything too.||||reg||1
Z||000010||turbo86se||10-31-2001||05:23 PM||||DRH, are you coming to Myrtle Beach anytime soon?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'll provide a place to stay, a turbo-charged Fiero to drive, and 18 holes of golf! LOL||||reg||7
Z||000011||DRH||10-31-2001||06:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by turbo86se:<BR><B>DRH, are you coming to Myrtle Beach anytime soon?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'll provide a place to stay, a turbo-charged Fiero to drive, and 18 holes of golf! LOL</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Afraid not  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I'm not much of a golfer anyway, driving the cart is the fun part for me! The turbo drive would be tempting if I were closer though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I became very familiar with the 88 front end last spring when I pulled the front subframe and replaced all the bushings, ball joints and bearings. <P>Make sure nothing is broken or bent to the point of breaking and you should be OK to drive a few miles to the shop.<P>||||reg||1
